config PMOVE
	tristate "Parallel Move — Dynamic Lane & Channel Assignment"
	depends on BLOCK && BLK_DEV
	select PROC_FS
	help
	  PMOVE provides a dedicated parallel move engine with independent
	  telemetry, abort capability, and move-specific optimizations.

	  Move strategy:
	    1. Attempt atomic do_renameat2() — O(1) inode swap (same-fs)
	    2. If -EXDEV: splice-based data migration + unlink (cross-device)
	    3. PMOVE_F_FORCE_COPY: always use splice path (benchmarking)

	  Dynamic assignment mirrors pcopy's engine:
	    - CPU load awareness (scales channels with available headroom)
	    - Device class speed constants shared with pcopy module
	    - PCIe lane utilization tracking
	    - File count proportional scaling

	  Reports move-specific metrics:
	    - Atomic renames (instant, zero data copy)
	    - Splice fallbacks (cross-device boundary detected)
	    - Bytes actually transferred (excludes instant renames)

	  Exposes:
	    /proc/pmove/status  - Hardware detection and dynamic state
	    /proc/pmove/config  - Tunable parameters
	    /dev/pmove          - ioctl interface for pmove tool

	  To compile as a module, choose M here: the module will be called pmove.

	  If unsure, say M.
